Fix AOT compatibility warnings in the following non-serialization files in `/tmp/sv-8ce2f743021f4ff2b303b4803a0e1f52/before/`. Do NOT run any builds - just make the edits.

## 1. Extensions/ArmClientBuilderExtensions.cs (line 30)
The method `AddArmClient<TBuilder, TConfiguration>` calls `builder.RegisterClientFactory` which has `[RequiresUnreferencedCode]` and `[RequiresDynamicCode]`. Add both attributes to the method:
```csharp
[RequiresUnreferencedCode("Binding strongly typed objects to configuration values is not supported with trimming. Use the Configuration Binder Source Generator (EnableConfigurationBindingGenerator=true) instead.")]
[RequiresDynamicCode("Binding strongly typed objects to configuration values requires generating dynamic code at runtime, for example instantiating generic types. Use the Configuration Binder Source Generator (EnableConfigurationBindingGenerator=true) instead.")]
```
The file already imports `System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis`.

## 2. GenericOperationSource.cs (lines 37, 40)
- Line 37: `ModelReaderWriter.Read(response.Content, typeof(T))` - the `typeof(T)` needs `[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.PublicConstructors | DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)]` on the class's generic parameter `T`.
- Line 40: `Activator.CreateInstance(typeof(T), ...)` - needs `NonPublicConstructors` on `T`.

Fix: Add the annotation to the class declaration's generic parameter:
```csharp
internal class GenericOperationSource<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.PublicConstructors | DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T> : IOperationSource<T>
```

## 3. ArmOperation.cs (lines 98, 104)
The `IsResource<T>()` method uses `typeof(T).GetConstructor(...)` and `Activator.CreateInstance(typeof(T), ...)`. Add `[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)]` to the type parameter `T` on `IsResource<T>()`:
```csharp
private static bool IsResource<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T>() where T : notnull
```

This will cascade: the callers `Rehydrate<T>` (line 44) and `RehydrateAsync<T>` (line 82) both call `IsResource<T>()`, so they also need the same annotation on their `T` parameter:
```csharp
public static ArmOperation<T> Rehydrate<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T>(ArmClient client, ...) where T : notnull
```
```csharp
public static async Task<ArmOperation<T>> RehydrateAsync<[DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors)] T>(ArmClient client, ...) where T : notnull
```

Also, `Rehydrate<T>` and `RehydrateAsync<T>` create `new GenericOperationSource<T>(client, isResource)` - and we just annotated GenericOperationSource with `PublicConstructors | NonPublicConstructors`. So the annotation on the Rehydrate methods needs to be the superset: `DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.PublicConstructors | DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.NonPublicConstructors`.

Add `using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;` to ArmOperation.cs (it doesn't have it).

## 4. ArmEnvironment.cs (line 80)
`public override string ToString() => JsonSerializer.Serialize(this);`

Replace with manual formatting that doesn't use JsonSerializer. ArmEnvironment has `Endpoint` (Uri) and `Audience` (string) properties. Use:
```csharp
public override string ToString() => $"{{\"Endpoint\":\"{Endpoint}\",\"Audience\":\"{Audience}\"}}";
```
This preserves the JSON-like output without requiring JsonSerializer. Also remove `using System.Text.Json;` if it's no longer needed (check if JsonSerializer is used elsewhere in the file first - it is NOT).

## 5. ArmClientOptions.cs (line 52)
`var allProfile = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>>(span);`

Replace with JsonDocument parsing:
```csharp
using var doc = JsonDocument.Parse(BinaryData.FromStream(stream));
var allProfile = doc.RootElement;
var armProfile = allProfile.GetProperty("resource-manager");
foreach (var keyValuePair in armProfile.EnumerateObject())
{
    var namespaceName = keyValuePair.Name;
    var element = keyValuePair.Value;

    foreach (var apiVersionProperty in element.EnumerateObject())
    {
        var apiVersion = apiVersionProperty.Name;
        foreach (var resourceTypeItem in apiVersionProperty.Value.EnumerateArray())
        {
            string resourceTypeName = default;
            foreach (var property in resourceTypeItem.EnumerateObject())
            {
                if (property.NameEquals("resourceType"))
                {
                    resourceTypeName = property.Value.GetString();
                    break;
                }
            }
            var resourceType = $"{namespaceName}/{resourceTypeName}";
            ResourceApiVersionOverrides[resourceType] = apiVersion;
        }
    }
}
```

The whole method body from `using (Stream stream = ...)` onwards needs refactoring. The current code reads the stream, deserializes to Dictionary, then iterates. Replace the body so we parse the document directly without deserializing to dictionary. Keep the `assembly.GetManifestResourceStream` call.

The new method body should be:
```csharp
public void SetApiVersionsFromProfile(AzureStackProfile profile)
{
    var assembly = Assembly.GetExecutingAssembly();
    using (Stream stream = assembly.GetManifestResourceStream(profile.GetManifestName()))
    {
        using var doc = JsonDocument.Parse(BinaryData.FromStream(stream));
        var armProfile = doc.RootElement.GetProperty("resource-manager");
        foreach (var keyValuePair in armProfile.EnumerateObject())
        {
            var namespaceName = keyValuePair.Name;
            var element = keyValuePair.Value;

            foreach (var apiVersionProperty in element.EnumerateObject())
            {
                var apiVersion = apiVersionProperty.Name;
                foreach (var resourceTypeItem in apiVersionProperty.Value.EnumerateArray())
                {
                    string resourceTypeName = default;
                    foreach (var property in resourceTypeItem.EnumerateObject())
                    {
                        if (property.NameEquals("resourceType"))
                        {
                            resourceTypeName = property.Value.GetString();
                            break;
                        }
                    }
                    var resourceType = $"{namespaceName}/{resourceTypeName}";
                    ResourceApiVersionOverrides[resourceType] = apiVersion;
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

Also remove `using System.Text.Json;` from ArmClientOptions.cs if JsonSerializer is no longer used (check - it is NOT used elsewhere). But keep `System.Text.Json` namespace if `JsonElement` or `JsonDocument` is still used... Actually `JsonDocument` and `JsonElement` are in `System.Text.Json`, so keep the using.

